<title>GERMANY: Krupp chief calls warnings of job cuts nonsense.</title>
<headline>Krupp chief calls warnings of job cuts nonsense.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Without directly confirming plans to launch a bid for rival Thyssen AG, Krupp chairman Gerhard Cromme told angry steelworkers on Tuesday that rumours of impending job cuts were nonsense.</p>
<p>Thyssen AG said late on Monday that it had information that Fried. Krupp AG Hoesch-Krupp planned a hostile takeover bid that could only be carried out with &quot;tens of thousands&quot; of job cuts in the steel industry.</p>
<p>&quot;The numbers that are making the rounds are complete nonsense,&quot; Cromme told a gathering of angry steel workers protesting the takeover plans in front of Krupp's headquarters in Essen.</p>
<p>Cromme, who was booed down by demonstrators, did not say whether the company actually planned to launch a bid for Thyssen.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
